  "claim": "The satellite International Ultraviolet Explorer was operational longer than EXOSAT.",
  "evidencia": "Page: International Ultraviolet Explorer. Sentence: The International Ultraviolet Explorer (IUE) was an astronomical observatory satellite primarily designed to take ultraviolet spectra.\nPage: International Ultraviolet Explorer. Sentence: The mission lifetime was initially set for 3 years, but in the end it lasted almost 18 years, with the satellite being shut down in 1996.\nPage: EXOSAT. Sentence: The European X-ray Observatory Satellite (EXOSAT), originally named HELOS, was an X-ray telescope operational from May 1983 until April 1986 and in that time made 1780 observations in the X-ray band of most classes of astronomical object including active galactic nuclei, stellar coronae, cataclysmic variables, white dwarfs, X-ray binaries, clusters of galaxies, and supernova remnants.",
